ystems so right now there's a race the  Russians are clearly violating and in  started the so-called race will continue  to abide by the treaty will conduct  research and development when and if  we're allowed to do so after the second  will always develop systems that help  protect our global interests for the  United States and working with our  partners and allies and this is a great  example of that if you look at the  situation right now that has  substantially changed and the situation  that was in the times of Cold War what  are the differences and similarities  between these two situations I could  probably do a couple more news shows  with you to describe the threat  environment I mean obviously technology  has changed partnerships have changed  the threat environment from radical  Islamic threat to state actors have  changed but fortunately we've got a  great team here and continue to assess  that we continue to work with our  partners DoD across the interagency and  partners and allies whether it be in the  Middle East Europe or globally around  the world to best protect those  interests I think that the situation the  a security situation right now is better  that the environment is more secure than  it was back in their times of the  I don't think you really can compare  contrast the worlds in two very  different places than we were in the  1980s and where we are today  again I've served a nation for over 30  years and in various war zones in  conflict areas and again there there are  threats there and we will continue to  mitigate those threats both with our  systems our people and work with our  partners and allies to best protect the  interests the secretary Thompson thank  you very much for the interview and best  of luck for you thanks so much for the  opportunity appreciate it thank you  you
 

